Subject: Autoload tests/ and plugin classes without a composer install

composer.json declares tests/ under autoload-dev's classmap, and every
plugin's own composer.json declares its own autoload.classmap (some just
their top-level <name>.php, others also a lib/ or drivers/ subdirectory -
see e.g. plugins/managesieve/composer.json, plugins/password/composer.json).
All of this only takes effect once `composer install` has generated
vendor/autoload.php. This package's Debian build doesn't do that - like
the rest of this package, it relies on system-installed PHP libraries
rather than a vendor/ tree - so phpunit fails immediately in its
bootstrap script ("Class Roundcube\Tests\ActionTestCase not found"),
and once that's worked around, every plugin test fails the same way on
its own plugin's classes.

tests/ classes follow a plain PSR-4 layout under the Roundcube\Tests
namespace (Roundcube\Tests\Framework\X lives at tests/Framework/X.php,
and so on), so a small spl_autoload_register callback mapping that
namespace onto TESTS_DIR reproduces exactly what composer's own generated
autoloader would have done there.

Plugin classes don't follow one single convention (contrast managesieve's
"lib/" with password's "drivers/" with example_addressbook's two explicit
files), so rather than hardcode each plugin's layout, a second
spl_autoload_register callback builds a classmap directly from every
plugin's own composer.json autoload.classmap entries - the same
authoritative metadata a real composer install would read - and reuses
whatever it finds.

Forwarded: not-needed
---
Index: rc-build/tests/bootstrap.php
===================================================================
--- rc-build.orig/tests/bootstrap.php
+++ rc-build/tests/bootstrap.php
@@ -42,6 +42,62 @@
 if (@is_dir(TESTS_DIR . 'config')) {
     define('RCUBE_CONFIG_DIR', TESTS_DIR . 'config');
 }
+
+// PSR-4 autoloading for Roundcube\Tests\* (composer's autoload-dev would
+// normally provide this via vendor/autoload.php - see PACKAGING-NOTES.md).
+spl_autoload_register(static function (string $class): void {
+    $prefix = __NAMESPACE__ . '\\';
+    if (!str_starts_with($class, $prefix)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    $file = TESTS_DIR . str_replace('\\', '/', substr($class, strlen($prefix))) . '.php';
+    if (is_readable($file)) {
+        require_once $file;
+    }
+});
+
+// Autoload plugin classes the same way composer's own generated autoloader
+// would: each plugin's composer.json declares its own autoload.classmap
+// (files and/or directories, e.g. plugins/managesieve/lib/), which is
+// exactly what would be merged into vendor/autoload.php's classmap by a
+// real composer install (see the Roundcube\Tests note above for why this
+// package's Debian build doesn't do that). Built from that same metadata
+// instead of hardcoding each plugin's layout so this doesn't drift.
+spl_autoload_register(static function (string $class): void {
+    static $classmap = null;
+    if ($classmap === null) {
+        $classmap = [];
+        $addFile = static function (string $file) use (&$classmap): void {
+            if (!is_readable($file)) {
+                return;
+            }
+            if (preg_match_all('/\\bclass\\s+(\\w+)/', file_get_contents($file), $m)) {
+                foreach ($m[1] as $name) {
+                    $classmap[$name] = $file;
+                }
+            }
+        };
+        foreach (glob(INSTALL_PATH . 'plugins/*/composer.json') as $composerFile) {
+            $paths = json_decode(file_get_contents($composerFile), true)['autoload']['classmap'] ?? [];
+            foreach ($paths as $path) {
+                $full = dirname($composerFile) . '/' . $path;
+                if (is_dir($full)) {
+                    $it = new \RecursiveIteratorIterator(new \RecursiveDirectoryIterator($full, \FilesystemIterator::SKIP_DOTS));
+                    foreach ($it as $fileInfo) {
+                        if ($fileInfo->getExtension() === 'php') {
+                            $addFile($fileInfo->getPathname());
+                        }
+                    }
+                } else {
+                    $addFile($full);
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    if (isset($classmap[$class])) {
+        require_once $classmap[$class];
+    }
+});
 
 // Some tests depend on the way phpunit is executed
 $_SERVER['SCRIPT_NAME'] = 'vendor/bin/phpunit';
